# 低频词汇 List07
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List07核心词汇

{{commence}}{/kəˈmens/}{开始；着手}{The ceremony will commence at 9 a.m. sharp.}}
{{commend}}{/kəˈmend/}{赞扬；推荐}{The teacher commended the student for excellent work.}}
{{commentary}}{/ˈkɒməntri/}{评论；解说}{The sports commentary was both entertaining and informative.}}
{{commerce}}{/ˈkɒmɜːs/}{商业；贸易}{E-commerce has transformed the landscape of global commerce.}}
{{commission}}{/kəˈmɪʃn/}{委员会；佣金}{She earns a commission on every sale she makes.}}
{{commodity}}{/kəˈmɒdəti/}{商品；日用品}{Oil is one of the most traded commodities in the world.}}
{{communal}}{/kəˈmjuːnl/}{公共的；集体的}{The building has a communal garden for all residents.}}
{{compact}}{/kəmˈpækt/}{紧凑的；压缩的}{The compact design makes it easy to carry.}}
{{comparable}}{/ˈkɒmpərəbl/}{可比较的；类似的}{The quality is comparable to higher-priced alternatives.}}
{{compassion}}{/kəmˈpæʃn/}{同情；怜悯}{She showed great compassion for the victims of the disaster.}}
{{compatible}}{/kəmˈpætəbl/}{兼容的；合得来的}{The two colleagues are very compatible in their work styles.}}
{{compel}}{/kəmˈpel/}{强迫；迫使}{The evidence compelled the court to change its ruling.}}
{{compensate}}{/ˈkɒmpenseɪt/}{补偿；赔偿}{The airline compensated passengers for the delayed flight.}}
{{compile}}{/kəmˈpaɪl/}{编辑；汇编}{The researcher compiled data from multiple sources.}}
{{complement}}{/ˈkɒmplɪment/}{补充；补足}{The new wing complements the original building perfectly.}}
{{compliance}}{/kəmˈplaɪəns/}{遵守；合规}{The company ensures compliance with all safety regulations.}}
{{complication}}{/ˌkɒmplɪˈkeɪʃn/}{并发症；复杂情况}{The surgery was successful without any complications.}}
{{comply}}{/kəmˈplaɪ/}{遵守；服从}{All vendors must comply with the company's code of conduct.}}
{{component}}{/kəmˈpəʊnənt/}{组成部分；零件}{Each component of the system must be tested individually.}}
{{comprehend}}{/ˌkɒmprɪˈhend/}{理解；领会}{It is difficult to comprehend the scale of the universe.}}
{{compulsory}}{/kəmˈpʌlsəri/}{强制的；必修的}{Mathematics is a compulsory subject in most schools.}}
{{compute}}{/kəmˈpjuːt/}{计算；估算}{The software can compute complex mathematical equations.}}
{{conceal}}{/kənˈsiːl/}{隐藏；隐瞒}{He tried to conceal his disappointment with a smile.}}
{{concede}}{/kənˈsiːd/}{承认；让步}{The candidate conceded defeat after the final count.}}
{{conceive}}{/kənˈsiːv/}{构想；怀孕}{She conceived a plan to improve efficiency.}}
{{condemn}}{/kənˈdem/}{谴责；判刑}{World leaders condemned the act of terrorism.}}
{{confess}}{/kənˈfes/}{承认；忏悔}{He confessed that he had made a serious error.}}
{{confidential}}{/ˌkɒnfɪˈdenʃl/}{机密的；保密的}{The documents are strictly confidential.}}
{{confine}}{/kənˈfaɪn/}{限制；禁闭}{The discussion was confined to the agenda items.}}
{{confirmation}}{/ˌkɒnfəˈmeɪʃn/}{确认；证实}{We are waiting for confirmation of the booking.}}
